<title>USA: General Electric unit gets engine contracts.</title>
<headline>General Electric unit gets engine contracts.</headline>
<dateline>EVANDALE, Ohio 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>GE Engine Services, a subsidiary of General Electric Co, said Thursday it has been awarded contracts from USAir Group Inc to maintain, repair and overhaul more than 300 engines used by the airline.</p>
<p>GE Engine Services is to maintain the CFM56-3 engines powering USAir's fleet of 139 Boeing Co 737-300 and 737-400s, as well as the CF6-80C2 engines powering USAir's 12 Boeing 767 aircraft.</p>
<p>The value of the contracts, which may be extended for up to 10 years, was not disclosed.</p>
</text>
